& [TrustModuleSet] is the executable boundary
  + [types] is signed package, recognition certificate, distinct authority and compiler statements, authority scopes, trust store, quotes, and read-only admitted package
  + [crypto] is canonical JSON hashing with SHA-256 and strict Ed25519 verification
  + [compiler] is deterministic sorting, exact indexing, stable semantic identity, byte-span capture, dual signing, and proof/dependency binding
  + [admission] is fail-closed identity, digest, root, signature, validity, revocation, staleness, compiler, dependency, scope, structure, index, reference, and exact-quote gates

& [AuthorityDecisionSet] is the implemented meaning
  + [recognition] is a Cantor Recognition Certificate rather than an error-detecting CRC checksum
  + [signature_roles] is authority approval and compiler attestation remain separately signed and separately trusted
  + [content_authority] is SHA-256 digests bind the canonical package, semantic root, source root, dependency lock, and proof identifiers
  + [source_authority] is exact quoted bytes must match both their signed source snapshot and span digest
  + [address_stability] is semantic unit identity survives line relocation while package identity and human-readable line coordinates change on recompilation
  + [immutability] is admitted packages expose read-only inspection methods and cannot be mutated through the admitted value
  + [self_reference] is package-address fields use a normalized pending identity during digest construction and must equal the final derived package identity at admission

& [DeliberateLimitationSet] is retained
  + [canonical_encoding] is deterministic serde_json over ordered Rust structures under the versioned compiler and dependency lock; cross-language canonical bytes require a separately frozen interchange profile
  + [separation_of_duty] is cryptographically distinct fixture keys and signer roles, not organizational isolation; the baseline compiler object holds both test signers
  + [key_material] is fixture keys exist only in tests; production key storage, rotation, ceremony, and HSM integration are absent
  + [serialization] is canonical JSON under the bound package format and compiler profile rather than a cross-language canonicalization standard
  + [revocation] is a supplied local trust-store decision rather than a network revocation service
  + [query] is not part of this slice and is activated separately as CEB Slice 03
  - never: treat content digest alone, unsigned packages, or a successful parse as authority

